Christian genealogy series.
This is the genealogy of Jesus Christ. He is the son of David, and also the son of Abraham.
Abraham was the father of Isaac. Isaac was the father of Jacob. Jacob was the father of Judah and his brothers.
Judah the father of Perez and Zerah, and their mother was Tamar. Perez the father of Hezron. Hezron the father of Ram.
Ram the father of Amminadab, and Amminadab the father of Nahshon, and Nahshon the father of Salmon.
Salmon father of Boaz. Rahab mother of Boaz. Boaz father of Obed. Ruth mother of Obed. Obed father of Jesse.
And Jesse was the father of King David. And David was the father of Solomon. And the mother of Solomon was the wife of Uriah.
Solomon the son of Rehoboam, and Rehoboam the son of Solomon, and Abijah the son of Rehoboam, and Asa the son of Abijah.
Asa was the father of Jehoshaphat. And Jehoshaphat was the father of Joram. And Joram was the father of Uzziah.
Uzziah the father of Jotham, Jotham the father of Ahaz, Ahaz the father of Hezekiah.
Hezekiah was the father of Manasseh. Manasseh was the father of Amon. Amon was the father of Josiah.
Josiah was the father of Jeconiah and his brothers. It was during this time that the Jewish people were exiled to Babylon.
And afterward the genealogy of the family continued. And Zerubbabel was the father of Shealtiel, and Shealtiel the father of Zerubbabel.
Zerubbabel was the father of Oded. Oded was the father of Eliakim. Eliakim was the father of Azra.
Azor was the father of Zadok. Zadok was the father of Aaim. Aaim was the father of Elioenai.
Eliud the father of Eleazar. And Eleazar the father of Mattai. And Mattai the father of Jacob.
Jacob was the father of Joseph. Joseph was the husband of Mary. And Mary gave birth to Jesus who is called the Christ.
There were fourteen generations from Abraham to David; and fourteen from David until the carrying away of Babylon the Jews; and fourteen from that time until Christ. The birth of Jesus Christ.
This is how the birth of Jesus Christ happened. His mother Mary was engaged to Joseph. But before they started living together, it became clear that she would give birth to a child. Mary was conceived by the Holy Spirit.
Her husband Joseph was a pious man. He did not want to embarrass her in front of people. Therefore, he planned to divorce her secretly.
While he was thinking over all this in his mind, suddenly an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream, saying, "Joseph son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary your wife into your home. For the child conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit."
She will give birth to a son. And you shall name him Jesus, because he will save his people from their sins.
All this was done so that what the Lord had said would happen. For he spoke this through the prophet,
Immanuel, which being interpreted means, God with us. (Isaiah 7:14)
Joseph woke up. And he did what the angel of the Lord commanded him. He took Mary into his house as his wife.
And he did not know her until she bore a son. And he called his name Jesus.
