Then Jesus left the crowd and went into the house. And the disciples came to Him and said, "Explain to us the parable of the tares of the field."
He answered them, "The one who sowed the good seed is the son of man."
The field is the world. The good seed represents the people who belong to the kingdom. The weeds are the people who belong to the enemy of good.
The enemy who sows them is the devil. And the harvest is the Day of Judgment. And the laborers are the angels.
The grass is uprooted and burned in the fire. So it will be on the day of reckoning.
The Son of Man will send his angels, and they will remove from his kingdom all causes of sin and those who practice evil.
They will cast them into the furnace of fire. There the people cry and gnash their teeth.
Then the awliya of Allah are filled with wonder in the kingdom of their father, just as the sun is filled with wonder in the firmament. They hear and obey. Is their example like the example of the treasure hidden and the pearl concealed in the sea?
The parable of the Kingdom of Heaven is like a treasure hidden in a field, which a man found; in his joy he went and sold all that he had and bought that field.
And another time, it is similar to the Kingdom of the Heavens is like a merchant of pearls who was seeking a very precious pearl.
He found one pearl of very great value; so he went and sold all that he possessed, and bought that pearl. The Tale of the Net.
And as we said once again, the kingdom of the heavens is like a net cast into the sea, which gathers of every kind.
When the net was full, the fishermen drew it to the shore. Then they sat down and took the good fish and put them in the baskets. But the bad fish they threw away.
This is what the Day of Judgment will be like. The angels will come. They will separate those who did evil from those who did good.
They will cast the wicked into the burning furnace. There they will weep and gnash their teeth, sorrowful.
Do you understand all these things? Jesus asked them. And they answered him, Yes.
