And after he had dismissed them, he went up into the mountain to pray by himself. And when evening came, he was there alone.
The boat was already far from the shore, and the waves were tossing it strongly because the wind was hitting against its direction.
Early in the morning, Jesus went out to the disciples. And He walked on the sea.
They saw him walking on the lake, and they were terrified. "A spirit!" they cried out, and they screamed in fright.
Jesus said to them immediately, "Be confident! I am. Do not be afraid."
"Master, are you he?" asked Peter. "If you are, command me to come to you on the water."
Jesus said, "Come." So Peter got out of the boat, and he walked on the water and he turned toward Jesus.
But when Peter saw the wind, he was afraid. And beginning to sink, he cried out, saying, "Lord, save me!"
And Jesus immediately stretched out his hand and grasped him, and said to him, "O you of little faith! Why did you doubt?"
When they climbed into the boat, the wind died down.
So they submitted and said, "In truth, you are the Son of God!"
They crossed the lake and disembarked at Capernaum.
And the men who were inhabitants of the place recognized him, so they sent to all the surrounding villages, and they brought to him everyone who was sick.
They asked him to allow only the sick to touch the edge of his garments. And everyone who touched him was healed.
